---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Premium from '../../components/en/Premium.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/en/Hero.astro';
import Insurance from '../../components/en/Insurance.astro';
const path='/en/health-insurance-acupuncture';
const faqs=[
 {q:'Can I buy supplementary insurance when I need treatment?',a:'Acceptance is not automatic. Insurers can require a health declaration, refuse an application or exclude pre-existing conditions. Do not assume a new policy will cover a current treatment need.'},
 {q:'Does an EMR or ASCA registration guarantee reimbursement?',a:'No. Recognition bodies assess practitioners, but your insurer decides which providers and methods it accepts under your policy. Confirm the individual practitioner and method before treatment.'},
 {q:'What if I have international insurance?',a:'Ask your insurer whether your plan covers outpatient complementary treatment in Switzerland, which practitioner qualifications it accepts, and what documents or advance authorisation it requires.'},
 {q:'Can I book without reimbursement?',a:'Ask the practice about self-payment, the full appointment fee and payment terms. An appointment request does not confirm either insurance coverage or a price.'},
];
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebPage',name:'Swiss health insurance for acupuncture and TCM',url:`https://tcm.ch${path}/`,inLanguage:'en'};
---
<Layout title="Swiss Health Insurance for Acupuncture & TCM | TCM.ch" description="Understand basic and supplementary insurance for acupuncture in Switzerland. Check the practitioner, treatment, policy limits and fees before booking." path={path} schema={schema}>
<Premium>
<Hero eyebrow="Insurance & costs" title="Understand your cover before you book." lead="For acupuncture and TCM, the practitioner, treatment and policy all matter. This guide helps you ask the right questions." primaryHref="#checklist" primaryLabel="Check your cover" secondaryHref="/en/contact/" secondaryLabel="Ask our team" />
<Insurance />
<section class="en-section" id="checklist"><div class="wrap en-split"><div><span class="en-label">Before your appointment</span><h2>Four things to confirm.</h2><p class="en-intro">Use the practitioner’s full name when contacting your insurer. The clinic brand alone is not enough.</p></div><ol class="en-list">
<li><strong>Your policy.</strong> Does it include the proposed complementary treatment? Ask about any exclusions or advance approval.</li>
<li><strong>Your practitioner.</strong> Is this individual recognised for this specific method?</li>
<li><strong>Your remaining benefit.</strong> Check annual limits, maximum reimbursable fees and your own share.</li>
<li><strong>Your invoice.</strong> Ask the practice about billing and the insurer how to submit the claim. Keep a copy of the itemised invoice.</li>
</ol></div></section>
<section class="en-section en-concrete"><div class="wrap en-split"><div><span class="en-label">Recognition</span><h2>EMR and ASCA, in plain English.</h2></div><div><p>EMR is the ErfahrungsMedizinisches Register, a Swiss quality register. ASCA is the Swiss Foundation for Complementary Medicine. Both assess practitioners against their recognition requirements.</p><p>These labels are useful checks, but they are not insurance policies. ASCA advises patients to check reimbursement with their insurer before starting treatment.</p><p class="en-note">Sources: <a href="https://emr.ch/de/das-emr">EMR</a> · <a href="https://asca.ch/de/ruckvergutung/">ASCA reimbursement guidance (German)</a></p></div></div></section>
<section class="en-section"><div class="wrap en-split"><div><span class="en-label">Common questions</span><h2>Make the costs clear.</h2><p>Ask the practice for the first-visit fee, expected duration and follow-up fees before agreeing to treatment.</p><a class="en-link" href="/en/knowledge/how-much-does-acupuncture-cost-in-switzerland/">Read our guide to costs →</a></div><div class="en-faq">{faqs.map(f=><details><summary>{f.q}</summary><p>{f.a}</p></details>)}<p class="en-note" style="margin-top:24px">Supplementary-insurance acceptance: <a href="https://www.helsana.ch/en/individuals/services/welcome.html">Helsana’s explanation for new customers</a>. Your own insurer’s decision and policy terms apply.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="en-section en-dark"><div class="wrap"><h2>Ready to discuss an appointment?</h2><p>Tell us your preferred location and what you would like to ask the practice.</p><a class="tcm-btn tcm-btn--mint" href="/en/contact/">Request an appointment ↗</a></div></section>
</Premium>
</Layout>
